# BaseMan - Cursor Rules

## Project Context
BaseMan is a Pac-Man arcade game remake with blockchain integration (Base + Farcaster Mini Apps).

## Key Technologies
- Farcaster Mini Apps SDK
- Base App Mini Apps SDK
- Neynar API (for user profiles)
- Ethereum/Ethers.js
- Base Blockchain (Mainnet & Sepolia)

## Neynar API Integration

### API Endpoint
- Base URL: `https://api.neynar.com`
- Endpoint: `/v2/farcaster/user/by/verified_address`
- Method: GET
- Headers:
  - `api_key: ${NEYNAR_API_KEY}`
  - `x-api-key: ${NEYNAR_API_KEY}`
  - `x-neynar-experimental: true`

### Usage in Project
- **File**: `api/_lib/farcaster-profiles.js`
- **Function**: `fetchNeynarProfile(address)`
- **Purpose**: Fetch user profile data (avatar, username, displayName) for leaderboard display

### API Response Format
The API returns user data in various formats. The `normalizeUser()` function handles:
- `user.pfp?.url` or `user.pfp_url` → avatarUrl
- `user.username` or `user.profile?.username` → username
- `user.display_name` or `user.displayName` → displayName
- `user.fid` → Farcaster ID

### Environment Variables
- `NEYNAR_API_KEY`: Required for API access
- `FARCASTER_PROFILE_PROVIDER`: Set to "neynar" or leave empty (default)

### Related Documentation
- Neynar API Docs: https://docs.neynar.com/
- Farcaster Mini Apps: https://miniapps.farcaster.xyz/
- Base Mini Apps: https://docs.base.org/mini-apps/

## Code Style
- Use async/await for API calls
- Always handle errors gracefully
- Use Map cache for profile data to avoid duplicate API calls
- Normalize addresses using `ethers.getAddress()`

## Important Files
- `api/leaderboard.js`: Leaderboard endpoint with profile enrichment
- `api/_lib/farcaster-profiles.js`: Neynar API integration
- `src/leaderboard-panel.js`: Frontend leaderboard display
- `src/profile-panel.js`: User profile panel

